─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
THEORY 7 FORMULATED: VM MEMORY STARVATION
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Analysis presented:
Without swap, kernel can't evict anonymous pages. When memory pressure
hits, only options:
- Evict page cache (etcd reads go to disk → slow)
- OOM kill processes (86 apiserver restarts, 44 etcd restarts)

"Chronic memory starvation cycle":
1. Memory pressure builds
2. kube-apiserver OOM-killed (biggest consumer)
3. Brief relief
4. apiserver restarts, allocates again
5. Cycle repeats

etcd's bbolt mmap'd DB:
- Needs page cache for performance
- 722 MB total buff/cache + DB ~200-500 MB → constant pressure
- Every evict → cold reads go to NVMe
- Explains slow-applies without hardware issue

"Revised timeline and root cause":
Background state: k8s-master1 runs K8s with only 2.2 GB RAM, 0 swap,
committed 4.7 GB → constant memory pressure → page cache thrashing
→ etcd IO is effectively random disk reads → chronic slow-applies
→ kube-apiserver OOM loop (86 restarts)

